ubscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2014-12-03T05:56:13Z","updated_at":"2014-12-03T06:14:06Z","body":"Explicit conversion operators are an unsupported C++11 feature in MSVC11 (Visual Studio 2012).\nSee http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/hh567368.aspx\n\nSorry at the time of the commit I didn't try it with previous MSVC versions. However it is a core C++11 feature, it seems Microsoft only adapted it in Visual Studio 2013.\n\nAfter a short research: it is supported by and above Visual C++ 2013 (MSVC12), GCC 4.5, Clang 3.0 and Intel C++ Composer XE 13.0.\n\nWe should release something like a 0.9.6.1 hotfix and enable this feature with some macro predefinition like GLM_FORCE_CPP11 for the present.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/g-truc/glm/issues/comments/65359626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"plasmacel","id":5353968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNTM5Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5353968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel","html_url":"https://github.com/plasmacel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/plasmacel/orgs","repos_u